A||||3||onfire||I need some help, on license plate frame suggestions. For a Nissan Pathfinder. Pics.||||2||
Z||000000||onfire||12-18-2001||04:36 AM||||Went four wheeling on Sunday. I in my Chevy s10 truck, My uncle in his Bronco II, and my friend in his Nissan Pathfinder.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4x4trip.jpg"> <P> We found out quick that the Nissan needs tires and a lift. As it kept getting stuck.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4x4stuck.jpg"> <P>This happened when my uncle pulled him out, one of the many timesmy friend got stuck. Luckily the bumper has open slots where it attacthes to the frame. So no real damage was done. Reattacthed in less than an hour. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4x4front.jpg"> <P>This happened when I pulled him out from the rear. I broke his frame, and bent the license plate pretty good. We flattened the plate back out. But he needs a new frame. So I need a few suggestions.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4x4rear.jpg"> <P>You know something like.<BR>"I am never going four wheeling with Aaron again."<BR>or <BR>"I went four wheelin' with Aaron, and all I got was this frame."<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.gif"> ||||reg||2
